{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat","id":772361,"title":"How to be a Buff Dispenser Sidereal Machine in Combat ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-23T09:20:51-08:00","id":772361,"title":"How to be a Buff Dispenser Sidereal Machine in Combat ?","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/YVNST0o.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> So I want to play a combat support type of Sidereal, I was going for the Defend Other route at first, either with Trouble Reduction Strategy or Crane Style, but the problem is that Sidereal can only add (Essence) to their DV, and my Sidereal has Essence 1, the TN reduction is useless in this case too, though you can go around this problem by throwing a bunch of penalty at your opponent, either through poison or social influence, sooooo, does anybody has any suggestion for the latter, Sorcery, MA or Evocation, I'm fine with anything (though I'm prefer effect that help a dodge Sidereal).<br /> <br /> Throne Shadow also help me with this concept, though I still don't understand how the capstone work in Ex2, and there are no rewrite for Ex3 yet, not to mention I'm not sure if the style will be a separate thing or got fold into Sidereal Brawl.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T10:02:47-08:00","id":772383,"title":"","content":"A: Your art is really pretty, I like the shirtless man with the hugely impractical axe.<br /> <br /> B: Throne Shadow Style will probably be it's own martial art, based on the facebook post by Mr. Morke<br /> <br /> C: A few people have been remaking Martial Arts for 3e, including me, you could check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/708919-everybody-was-kung-fu-fighting-share-your-martial-arts\">this</a> thread to see if there's anything you might find useful.<br /> <br /> D: If all else fails, I could try and make an adaption of Throne Shadow Style, if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T10:23:45-08:00","id":772392,"title":"","content":"Astrology.<br /> <br /> If you want to be a buffbot/support Sidereal, astrology is your best friend and lover.<br /> <br /> Just give your GM $50 or a couple of pizzas so that they let you replace Paradox with something that isn't pants-on-head. Like getting up and slamming your fingers in the door every time you make an astrology roll. That would be less painful and more conductive to good gameplay than Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T10:53:28-08:00","id":772404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772392#post772392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like getting up and slamming your fingers in the door every time you make an astrology roll. That would be less painful and more conductive to good gameplay than Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>But...but...what if that then ruins the art skills. A world without Jen-Art is a sadder and less beautiful world. T^T<br /> <br /> Also, really like the monster arm guy with hooves. &lt;3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T10:55:10-08:00","id":772407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanandithras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772404#post772404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, really like the monster arm guy with hooves. &lt;3</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Monstrous Husband Club Unites !<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772383#post772383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A: Your art is really pretty, I like the shirtless man with the hugely impractical axe.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>He's the party Taoist Twilight Sorcerer in fact x'D And since Artifacts are as light as feather I don't think that they are really that impractical, aren't they ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772383#post772383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> B: Throne Shadow Style will probably be it's own martial art, based on the facebook post by Mr. Morke<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, wasn't the FB post about MA Style mostly a joke thing, I vaguely remembered Morke said that they aren't actually spoiler for future stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772383#post772383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> D: If all else fails, I could try and make an adaption of Throne Shadow Style, if you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be amazing, yes !<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772392#post772392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Astrology.<br /> <br /> If you want to be a buffbot/support Sidereal, astrology is your best friend and lover.<br /> <br /> Just give your GM $50 or a couple of pizzas so that they let you replace Paradox with something that isn't pants-on-head. Like getting up and slamming your fingers in the door every time you make an astrology roll. That would be less painful and more conductive to good gameplay than Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you create destiny while not having access to the Loom of Fate ? Since my Sidereal is a special snowflake who never interact with Heaven.........","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 11-23-2015, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T11:57:38-08:00","id":772435,"title":"","content":"If you're the adorable pink haired one in the backdrop wielding the teacup, I think I might have an idea to go with that style ? It takes a little mixing and matching but can be thematically quite fun.<br /> <br /> Firstly, start with Optimistic Security Practice. In your rosy cheeks they see everything that they love and care about and have to be willing to strike that down before they can let their sword arm bring you harm ! Combine that with early Compassion style (Art of Victorious Concession) from Imperfect Lotus and you heroically stand in for your dear friends, softening the force of their cruel intentions. The kicker here is to then mix in a little black claw (ink monkies) so they and everyone else sees their wicked ways, and recognizes them for the monsters they are. Your shiny doe eyes stand as the last bastion as you selflessly impose yourself between the sinfulness of their hateful presumptions and your dear friends, while you offer them nothing but kind hugs to let your love burn away at them from the inside out.<br /> <br /> All this selfless subterfuge also mixes in wonderfully with You and Yours stance, and for the heck of it, you can Shun the Smiling Lady as a just revenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T12:17:11-08:00","id":772447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772407#post772407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you create destiny while not having access to the Loom of Fate ? Since my Sidereal is a special snowflake who never interact with Heaven.........</div> </div> </div> </div>There's two things at work here. Creating a capital-D Destiny [as per the background] requires the Loom of Fate. A lower-case d destiny, aka an astrological blessing or curse, is a smaller, shorter-lived enhancement, and only requires contact with the beneficiary when complete; a Destiny lasts until complete, an astrological blessing or curse lasts for as long as the successes dedicated to duration [as opposed to effect and scope] state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T12:19:11-08:00","id":772449,"title":"","content":"First thought: That's a big staff.<br /> <br /> Second thought: Oh not a staff, that's a big goremaul.<br /> <br /> Third thought: Wait no... that's a really big grimcleaver!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T12:40:19-08:00","id":772466,"title":"","content":"In-combat buffs seem to lovely be the province of Sorcery (though they mostly seem to be self-buffs).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure the game really mechanically supports &quot;in-combat buffbot&quot; as a concept beyond giving friends motes/Willpower with Solar Lore or the somewhat limited/very short duration stuff like Empowering Shout. Doing astrological stuff has never been that quick to execute. Generally, Exalts seem to be built to buff themselves. <br /> <br /> Now, I can see Sidereals being wicked debuffers as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T12:44:52-08:00","id":772469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772407#post772407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you create destiny while not having access to the Loom of Fate ? Since my Sidereal is a special snowflake who never interact with Heaven.........</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. To complete what yuurei said : you create it by petitioning the pattern spiders which is a prayer that can be accomplished from anywhere a normal prayer can<br /> <br /> Also not a single enhencement &quot;subtask&quot; requires having acces to heaven, though it might help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T12:58:50-08:00","id":772473,"title":"","content":"I like the DFO priests","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T13:10:11-08:00","id":772480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772449#post772449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First thought: That's a big staff.<br /> <br /> Second thought: Oh not a staff, that's a big goremaul.<br /> <br /> Third thought: Wait no... that's a really big grimcleaver!</div> </div> </div> </div>There is also a big goremaul that I thought was a big staff at first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T15:59:55-08:00","id":772582,"title":"","content":"I have nothing useful to add... I just love the art (the guy with the goremaul is my favorite) and I want to see more!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8764-zulkir-jhor","name":"Zulkir Jhor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T16:30:23-08:00","id":772615,"title":"","content":"Is this for 3e? If yes, Silver Voiced Nightingale is your friend. Crane is also helpful, for the reflexive defend other and counter-attacks. Not sure how well a Sidereal is going to work without their native charmset being out...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T21:46:03-08:00","id":772804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kawaiiwolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772435#post772435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're the adorable pink haired one in the backdrop wielding the teacup, I think I might have an idea to go with that style ? It takes a little mixing and matching but can be thematically quite fun.<br /> <br /> Firstly, start with Optimistic Security Practice. In your rosy cheeks they see everything that they love and care about and have to be willing to strike that down before they can let their sword arm bring you harm ! Combine that with early Compassion style (Art of Victorious Concession) from Imperfect Lotus and you heroically stand in for your dear friends, softening the force of their cruel intentions. The kicker here is to then mix in a little black claw (ink monkies) so they and everyone else sees their wicked ways, and recognizes them for the monsters they are. Your shiny doe eyes stand as the last bastion as you selflessly impose yourself between the sinfulness of their hateful presumptions and your dear friends, while you offer them nothing but kind hugs to let your love burn away at them from the inside out.<br /> <br /> All this selfless subterfuge also mixes in wonderfully with You and Yours stance, and for the heck of it, you can Shun the Smiling Lady as a just revenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any ways to dodge the Love Intimacy inflict by Black Claw Style when you learn it ? And I'm not sure how to explain where did she manage to learn this style since she has only Exalted for a month or so. Those burly Solar are the first chosen that she met so she can probably learn it from one of them, but that's......kinda creepy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772466#post772466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure the game really mechanically supports &quot;in-combat buffbot&quot; as a concept beyond giving friends motes/Willpower with Solar Lore or the somewhat limited/very short duration stuff like Empowering Shout. Doing astrological stuff has never been that quick to execute. Generally, Exalts seem to be built to buff themselves.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure about that, Solar Performance alone has 3 charms that are basically buff aura, there is also that one Evocation from the starmetal armor (Banging the Drum or something?). There is also Silver Voiced which has a bunch of supporting charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772466#post772466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I can see Sidereals being wicked debuffers as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is always Spring Razor if I just want to pile on a bunch of penalty on people, though I wonder if I can somehow fluff it into another type of equipment i.e A green jade toad statue that shoot out poisonous fume.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772473#post772473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the DFO priests</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it because they are a bunch of big daddies or.........?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772615#post772615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this for 3e? If yes, Silver Voiced Nightingale is your friend. Crane is also helpful, for the reflexive defend other and counter-attacks. Not sure how well a Sidereal is going to work without their native charmset being out...</div> </div> </div> </div>Errrggh, Silver Voiced Nightingale, I never like the style ever since I saw its illustration in SotM i.e Iron Siaka unfemininely shouting at someone, the style is basically hard-wired in to my head as &quot;Screaming like a Thug&quot; Style forever now.<br /> <br /> Crane is...nice, but all those +PDV is a waste when the Sidereal cap for DV is (Essence), plus they already has a reflexive defend other charm in Dodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T21:54:14-08:00","id":772808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772804#post772804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any ways to dodge the Love Intimacy inflict by Black Claw Style when you learn it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Take Duck Fate and bribe your GM with a few more pizzas.<br /> <br /> Bribing your GM with food is a good all-around strategy in most cases, actually.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T22:02:13-08:00","id":772814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772804#post772804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Errrggh, Silver Voiced Nightingale, I never like the style ever since I saw its illustration in SotM i.e Iron Siaka unfemininely shouting at someone, the style is basically hard-wired in to my head as &quot;Screaming like a Thug&quot; Style forever now.</div> </div> </div> </div>With 3e's revision that you can learn a version using instruments instead of voice, try this for inspiraton: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_v2thkzUolI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_v2thkzUolI</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T22:02:18-08:00","id":772815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772808#post772808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Take Duck Fate and bribe your GM with a few more pizzas.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal can dodge Intimacy ? Must be why they always so smug all the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772814#post772814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With 3e's revision that you can learn a version using instruments instead of voice, try this for inspiraton: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_v2thkzUolI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_v2thkzUolI</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know that you can use instrument with the Style in Ex3, my gripe is mostly that I can't get the image of SotM's Iron Siaka out of my mind which kinda ruin the whole Style for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 11-24-2015, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T22:16:54-08:00","id":772821,"title":"","content":"Nah, barring the ST just letting you, you can't<i> not</i> get the intimacy of love to your Sifu for BCS. That doesn't mean it has to be a romantic love, it can be the love one holds towards a parent or a teacher or the love one holds to their close sibling. I love my mother and my sister, I don't want to slip it to either of them, god help me.<br /> <br /> And depending on how cold hearted you want to be, an intimacy of love for someone doesn't mean it's impossible to kill them. Just difficult and you'd need stronger intimacies to support the murder of your beloved sifu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T22:42:36-08:00","id":772827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772407#post772407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's the party Taoist Twilight Sorcerer in fact x'D And since Artifacts are as light as feather I don't think that they are really that impractical, aren't they ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Slight point. Attunement doesn't make all artifacts 'light as a feather', it just makes them light enough to be lifted by the attuner. If you're waving a Grimcleaver sized for a Warstrider, you're probably going to still have something that weighs 200+ pounds AFTER Attunement. What I'm saying is make feat of strength rolls and get creative with environmental hazards.<br /> <br /> I am sad that you can't quite get into the mindset of Nightingale Style, since there's a lot of fun stuff in Ex3 for it. Like singing anthems to give allies bonuses on Join Battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T00:04:19-08:00","id":772853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772815#post772815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereal can dodge Intimacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>They absolutely can. Duck Fate lets them avoid any undesirable effect; if you don't want your character to have the mandatory intimacy from Black Claw Style, that is therefore an undesirable effect and a legal target to be dodged with Duck Fate.<br /> <br /> Honestly, half the fun of playing a Sidereal is rules lawyering and bullshitting your way into having your powers applicable in as many situations as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T00:26:46-08:00","id":772860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772466#post772466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In-combat buffs seem to lovely be the province of Sorcery (though they mostly seem to be self-buffs).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure the game really mechanically supports &quot;in-combat buffbot&quot; as a concept beyond giving friends motes/Willpower with Solar Lore or the somewhat limited/very short duration stuff like Empowering Shout. Doing astrological stuff has never been that quick to execute. Generally, Exalts seem to be built to buff themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having tried to play a support character, this is generally sad but true. Exalted mechanics very much tend towards the selfish, and options to empower others are limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T02:22:50-08:00","id":772887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772853#post772853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They absolutely can. Duck Fate lets them avoid any undesirable effect; if you don't want your character to have the mandatory intimacy from Black Claw Style, that is therefore an undesirable effect and a legal target to be dodged with Duck Fate.<br /> <br /> Honestly, half the fun of playing a Sidereal is rules lawyering and bullshitting your way into having your powers applicable in as many situations as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you Duck Fate against gaining the intimacy, you cannot learn the charms of Black Claw Style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T04:51:43-08:00","id":772959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772860#post772860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having tried to play a support character, this is generally sad but true. Exalted mechanics very much tend towards the selfish, and options to empower others are limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I feel sidereals have more tools to help them fit this role :<br /> - their anima effect is shared<br /> - Lots of charms, both in 2 and 2.5 ed :<br /> - a climate-changing charm that allows to help your allies with environmental effects<br /> - a ride charm that help find a path for you and your firends<br /> - the thrown charm that lets your ranged allies get a free reroll on their attacks<br /> - A linguistic charm that allows you to share languages with allies<br /> - the &quot;wedding&quot; charm that lets you take hits in place of your mate<br /> - a performance charm to improve stunt dices in a specific context<br /> - Performance also has a powerful willpower regeneration tool.<br /> - a socialize charm that allows you to &quot;craft&quot; a relationship of submisson between two persons (the master being one of your friends)<br /> - dodge-based defend other, and the option to use your dodge charms on their behalf<br /> - the archery pinacle charm thet lets you heal allies or grand them overdrive motes with your arrows<br /> - A melee charm that lets your &quot;students&quot; use your overdrive pool as if it was their own<br /> - Presence in abscence that lets you &quot;hijack&quot; other people's social interaction, possibly to enhace it (on a sidenote to devs : please please, keep this charm as is in 3ed. Thank you)<br /> - Sidereal shell-games or tought-swiping technique. Buff your allies by debuffing the enemy.<br /> - Avoiding the truth technique : pose as a liar to help your allies convince the target.<br /> - the stealth charm that gives arcane-fate to your friends<br /> - 2 awareness charms that help notice ambushes and unexpected attacks for your allies<br /> - integrity allows you to boost your allies' MDV<br /> - Didn't even mention medecine, sail and war since these abilites are strongly tied with working with a team<br /> - A few resplendency charms also allow you to bost or reroll social attacks/defense, boost willpower regeneration, training effects, talisman-creating effects, effects that help succeding valor rolls for people &quot;under your command&quot;.<br /> <br /> I would also add, but it's not specifically sidereal, though probably easier for them : there is a sidereal hearthstone (rating 3 iirc) that allows to force a reroll on anyone present in the scene (and you chose which result is kept so you can screw with enemy rolls just as efficiently as protecting your allies from unfortunate rolls). It also alows you to substract health levels of damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T05:13:08-08:00","id":772978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772466#post772466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In-combat buffs seem to lovely be the province of Sorcery (though they mostly seem to be self-buffs).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure the game really mechanically supports &amp;quot;in-combat buffbot&amp;quot; as a concept beyond giving friends motes/Willpower with Solar Lore or the somewhat limited/very short duration stuff like Empowering Shout. Doing astrological stuff has never been that quick to execute. Generally, Exalts seem to be built to buff themselves. <br /> <br /> Now, I can see Sidereals being wicked debuffers as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the DB book doesn't have more buff charms than personal charms I'll be disappointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T06:03:42-08:00","id":773028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772887#post772887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you Duck Fate against gaining the intimacy, you cannot learn the charms of Black Claw Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>It never says that in the style description, and not a single Charm in the style has the &quot;Prerequisite: Must have tie of love to Sifu&quot; to learn or use them. You learn the Style, it attempts to impose the intimacy on you, you Duck Fate it and walk off laughing because you're No Intimacy Having O'Toole. Yes, it does say that the intimacy cannot be removed, but you're still No Intimacy Having O'Toole because you used Duck Fate and it was never applied in the first place. There's also nothing to indicate that Black Claw Style is constantly or even periodically running an emotional checksum on you to make sure you still have the intimacy. The most protection it has is that it can't be completely removed, which of course is not a problem for our Sidereal because they never had the intimacy in the first place thanks to Duck Fate.<br /> <br /> Again, half the point of Sidereals is that they are rules lawyers on the cosmic scale. If one of them can use Martial Arts to literally block the Mark of Saturn, made by Saturn, than using Duck Fate to avoid the undesirable intimacy that comes with Black Claw Style (which is the entire point of the Charm!) seems like diminutive starchy root vegetables","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T06:15:05-08:00","id":773041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772449#post772449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First thought: That's a big staff.<br /> <br /> Second thought: Oh not a staff, that's a big goremaul.<br /> <br /> Third thought: Wait no... that's a really big grimcleaver!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I thought! How does that thing fit inside anything smaller than a palace?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T06:17:31-08:00","id":773043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772853#post772853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They absolutely can. Duck Fate lets them avoid any undesirable effect; if you don't want your character to have the mandatory intimacy from Black Claw Style, that is therefore an undesirable effect and a legal target to be dodged with Duck Fate.<br /> <br /> Honestly, half the fun of playing a Sidereal is rules lawyering and bullshitting your way into having your powers applicable in as many situations as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less Rules Lawyering and more &quot;Creative Interpretation&quot;. I loved that bit of 1st ed Sids.<br /> ... Now how can I use that particular skill to get Sids 3 into my hands NOW ?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T06:38:22-08:00","id":773057,"title":"","content":"I'd allow it on a starting character because it puts the PC in basically the same boat as someone whose beloved sifu suffered a nasty case of death by backstory.<br /> I'm more likely to be bothered by it happening in-game where we're actually roleplaying out the training scenes because under most circumstances I'd take an action like this as a sign of a deeper trust issue.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T07:51:34-08:00","id":773109,"title":"","content":"... But seriously, OP. Is this for 2e or 3e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T07:54:34-08:00","id":773110,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772804#post772804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there any ways to dodge the Love Intimacy inflict by Black Claw Style when you learn it ? And I'm not sure how to explain where did she manage to learn this style since she has only Exalted for a month or so. Those burly Solar are the first chosen that she met so she can probably learn it from one of them, but that's......kinda creepy.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772853#post772853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, half the fun of playing a Sidereal is rules lawyering and bullshitting your way into having your powers applicable in as many situations as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if there's no &quot;Non-shenanigan&quot; way to get past the intimacy of love then lets approach the problem like a sidereal ... <i>THINK SIDEWAYS</i> ! Feelings for someone in your party are no good by virtue of creepy and there's no sifu in the sky. But there could be one in your dreams ? Or even ones in your memory. I don't see a problem being enamored with a romantic notion from days long gone, lived in another life ? That romantic ideal is all in your head and who's to say that the real source could ever live up to the fantasy ! You could even double down and learn it from not just a figment in the past but your past self, introducing an unbreakable intimacy of narcissism !<br /> <br /> And ... lets be honest, look at those cheeks. Each time you see yourself in a mirror, puddle or shiny surface, would it really be so out of character to sigh wistfully or pass on a private wink ^_~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T07:54:55-08:00","id":773113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=773109#post773109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... But seriously, OP. Is this for 2e or 3e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ex3 of course, who even play Ex2 anymore :'P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T08:03:37-08:00","id":773118,"title":"","content":"Okay so you are already in &quot;houserule territory.&quot; That can be worked with.<br /> 1) Can you start with Martial Arts charms above Essence 1? Alternatively: are you getting a supernal at all?<br /> 2) How is your access to Mastery going to be handled?<br /> 3) How is Astrology going to work, if it's even a thing?<br /> 4) Are there any charm updates you are using? Is it upon request?<br /> 5) How is your anima banner going to be working?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T08:16:17-08:00","id":773130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=773118#post773118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) How is your anima banner going to be working?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C3_nxXDkU94\" data-code=\"C3_nxXDkU94\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/C3_nxXDkU94/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T12:55:46-08:00","id":773356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772821#post772821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, barring the ST just letting you, you can't<i> not</i> get the intimacy of love to your Sifu for BCS. That doesn't mean it has to be a romantic love, it can be the love one holds towards a parent or a teacher or the love one holds to their close sibling. I love my mother and my sister, I don't want to slip it to either of them, god help me.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I'm a cute Sidereal, and these are my five Solar papas! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T14:47:54-08:00","id":773440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772821#post772821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, barring the ST just letting you, you can't<i> not</i> get the intimacy of love to your Sifu for BCS. That doesn't mean it has to be a romantic love, it can be the love one holds towards a parent or a teacher or the love one holds to their close sibling. I love my mother and my sister, I don't want to slip it to either of them, god help me.<br /> <br /> And depending on how cold hearted you want to be, an intimacy of love for someone doesn't mean it's impossible to kill them. Just difficult and you'd need stronger intimacies to support the murder of your beloved sifu.</div> </div> </div> </div>An evil older sister-sifu seems like the perfect thing for this character. Complications!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T07:14:03-08:00","id":773929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=773440#post773440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An evil older sister-sifu seems like the perfect thing for this character. Complications!</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe sempai will notice me now ? N-not that I ~WANT them to, baka.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T07:55:40-08:00","id":773966,"title":"","content":"I think I have found the right build for her, go with Trouble Reduction Strategy (but I'm not sure how to properly transfer it to Ex3), take Snake Style, the first charm is more expensive than just using the Excellency, but what I want is the Form, -3 to the enemy's attack, dogpile on them with the TN increase from Blinding the Boar and some hypothetical Sid charm that prey on their 1s means that most opponents will have to burn a bunch of mote if they want to hit you.<br /> <br /> Though I'm not sure how much will it hurt if she is managed to get punch in the face, since Snake Style only allow light armor. And I need to find a way to transfer all those Initiative to the Solar somehow, using the Distract gambit is troublesome for the Sid, since it resets you to base Initiative which screw up the penalty inflict by Snake Form unless she can climb up the Initiative ladder fast. There is also Silver Voiced Nightingale, but the charm is post-Form so no dipping, and you can only transfer (Essence) point of Initiative , which mean only 1 in the case of this Sid. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=773440#post773440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An evil older sister-sifu seems like the perfect thing for this character. Complications!</div> </div> </div> </div>Older sister ? I think that the chance of a Celestial Exalted having a family member who is also a Celestial Exalted seems extremely low.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:30:09-08:00","id":773989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=773966#post773966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I have found the right build for her, go with Trouble Reduction Strategy (but I'm not sure how to properly transfer it to Ex3), take Snake Style, the first charm is more expensive than just using the Excellency, but what I want is the Form, -3 to the enemy's attack, dogpile on them with the TN increase from Blinding the Boar and some hypothetical Sid charm that prey on their 1s means that most opponents will have to burn a bunch of mote if they want to hit you.<br /> <br /> Though I'm not sure how much will it hurt if she is managed to get punch in the face, since Snake Style only allow light armor. And I need to find a way to transfer all those Initiative to the Solar somehow, using the Distract gambit is troublesome for the Sid, since it resets you to base Initiative which screw up the penalty inflict by Snake Form unless she can climb up the Initiative ladder fast. There is also Silver Voiced Nightingale, but the charm is post-Form so no dipping, and you can only transfer (Essence) point of Initiative , which mean only 1 in the case of this Sid.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Older sister ? I think that the chance of a Celestial Exalted having a family member who is also a Celestial Exalted seems extremely low.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Adopted Older Sister?<br /> <br /> Maybe a similar relationship that Mikoto and the Obsidian Lord in <a href=\"http://mai.wikia.com/wiki/Mai-HiME\" target=\"_blank\">Mai Hime</a> (without the mind control)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 11-25-2015, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:20:07-08:00","id":774358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=773966#post773966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Older sister ? I think that the chance of a Celestial Exalted having a family member who is also a Celestial Exalted seems extremely low.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thinking more of an adoptive scenario. Just as her Solar daddies aren't actually her <i>fathers</i>, her evil sister is actually her Black Claw sifu for whom she feels conflicted sisterly love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T21:01:05-08:00","id":774521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=774358#post774358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sisterly love.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, the fluff makes a big deal about Mara's nature leaking through the whole style (she can even access the Mastery tier), so I always assume the intimacy of Love must be a sexual one instead of warm fluzzy feeling in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T21:31:37-08:00","id":774532,"title":"","content":"I'm sure if Mara herself is teaching you it's most def gonna be a more sexual tone of love than otherwise. However the style only says that you can't learn it without being exposed to and accepting your sifu into your heart, but it says nothing about accepting them into your bed as well. Backing that up is how the Red Rule is explicitly there to let you shut any attempt to force your character down that road down, <i>and shut it down hard</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T21:39:40-08:00","id":774538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=774521#post774521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, the fluff makes a big deal about Mara's nature leaking through the whole style (she can even access the Mastery tier), so I always assume the intimacy of Love must be a sexual one instead of warm fluzzy feeling in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly what CoL says. It just says there's an unavoidable Intimacy of Love, but it doesn't say a THING about what kind of love it is. If she was taught by say, another Sidereal who was a bit older than her, she can say &quot;Oh, she's basically my older sister, and I love her! &lt;3&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T03:36:44-08:00","id":774646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=774521#post774521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, the fluff makes a big deal about Mara's nature leaking through the whole style (she can even access the Mastery tier), so I always assume the intimacy of Love must be a sexual one instead of warm fluzzy feeling in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>As said, there's no requirement other than &quot;love.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is not to say that it can't be weird and dark and maybe a little bit sexualized <i>anyway</i>, because you're already running on a bara aesthetic; some contrasting yuri undertones aren't out of the question.<br /> <br /> It's, like, a free recurring antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T03:52:49-08:00","id":774656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=773966#post773966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Older sister ? I think that the chance of a Celestial Exalted having a family member who is also a Celestial Exalted seems extremely low.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd put the chances of that happening in the same range as a circle of 5 similar buff Solars exalting into a circle. Which is still a better chance of happening than the same lot becoming daddies to a lost little Sid girl. I'd say that you'd be quite fine to add a Sister into the mix <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T05:12:02-08:00","id":774689,"title":"","content":"I attempted to turn Trouble Reduction Strategy into a 3e Charm, I am not sure how balanced it is, but I hope it can be of use.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Trouble Reduction Strategy</b></span></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Dodge 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Absence<br /> <br /> Generous Sidereals learn to spot impending danger to others, protecting the people around them even as they escape danger themselves.<br /> Whenever an ally within short range of the Exalt is attacked, she may reflexively perform a Defend Other action on them, using her Dodge score to defend her allies in place of her Parry score, in addition, if she has a positive intimacy towards the person she is defending or something that person represents, she may add one to that score. This only applies to the Defend Other Action and does not increase her own Dodge score. She may only use this Charm on one ally at a time.<br /> If the Sidereal activates Avoidance Kata while one of her allies is within close range of her, she may spend an additional willpower to take this ally with her to this new location. The target has to be willing to be taken along.<br /> At Essence 3, The Exalt may purchase this Charm a second time. Upon doing so, she may use it to reflexively defend any number of ally within short range. She pays the full cost of this Charm per ally that she defends. The Sidereal may now also take multiple people along when using Avoidance Kata, spending one willpower per character she takes along with her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","user":"While My Guitar","date":". 11-26-2015, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T07:02:14-08:00","id":774761,"title":"","content":"3 motes, lasts only a one action and gives you very limited bonuses. Seems weak.<br /> <br /> Didn't the version from 2.5 allow you to do reflexive defend other action and cost only 1 mote per target defended?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T07:16:22-08:00","id":774769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=774761#post774761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 motes, lasts only a one action and gives you very limited bonuses. Seems weak.<br /> <br /> Didn't the version from 2.5 allow you to do reflexive defend other action and cost only 1 mote per target defended?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is correct, but in the new system, the Defend Other action is quite powerful. And spending 1 mote per character that you defend seems overpowered to me.<br /> You might be right that it is underpowered in it's current form though.<br /> <br /> Edit: Has been adjusted, it's now reflexive, but I think it might be too good right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","user":"While My Guitar","date":". 11-26-2015, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T08:55:06-08:00","id":774842,"title":"","content":"I agree that it may be too good to grant a reflexive defend other in the new combat paradigm.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, buying one (or two) charms and paying an upfront cost of 3*x motes and possibly have it be useless because either :<br /> - some of your targets are not attacked<br /> - some of your targets are not in range when attacked<br /> <br /> That sucks.<br /> <br /> So what I would advise to at least change it that way :<br /> - The charm is reflexive and is activated only when your target is attacked (he keeps the benefit of this charm until the end of the defend other action)<br /> - if you repurchase the charm you can declare a special &quot;dodge defend other&quot; action without specifying a target. Everytime someone in your defend other range gets attacked you can opt to defend him by paying 3 motes (each person keeps the benefit of the charm for the duration of the whole defend other action)<br /> <br /> It costs the same, basically works the same, except you can't waste motes for nothing because you only pay when needed, and only once per target per turn.<br /> <br /> Aditionally, I would grant this charm another effect to give it more appeal (especially the non-repurchase version that looks weak) :<br /> Since it's an unconventional &quot;dodge-based defend other&quot; I would add that attackers need to succeed at a perception+awareness roll against some difficulty (your dodge rating? stealth? larceny? a contested roll of your manipulation + dodge?) to notice that you actually helped in defending the target.<br /> <br /> I think it would be nice and fitting for sidereals to defend people without anyone noticing they were involved, like an old lady that crosses the combat ground and &quot;unintentionally&quot; hinders the attackers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":2172,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","user":"Jack In The Box","date":". 11-26-2015, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T18:16:26-08:00","id":775129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=772804#post772804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is always Spring Razor if I just want to pile on a bunch of penalty on people, though I wonder if I can somehow fluff it into another type of equipment i.e A green jade toad statue that shoot out poisonous fume.</div> </div> </div> </div>A poisonous <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iFiiXkonsXY\" target=\"_blank\">kendama </a><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kendama\" target=\"_blank\">hammer-and-ball</a> that is mechanically identical to a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/763801-chain-and-rope-weaponry-peach\">yo-yo</a>? Or just a yo-yo.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Errrggh, Silver Voiced Nightingale, I never like the style ever since I saw its illustration in SotM i.e Iron Siaka unfemininely shouting at someone, the style is basically hard-wired in to my head as &quot;Screaming like a Thug&quot; Style forever now. </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the solution is to find a strong visual image to help you overwrite that impression.<br /> <br /> A character who fights with music and voice and inspiration, without shouting like a thug.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I don't have something in mind at this moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T19:44:08-08:00","id":775181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=775129#post775129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like the solution is to find a strong visual image to help you overwrite that impression.<br /> <br /> A character who fights with music and voice and inspiration, without shouting like a thug.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I don't have something in mind at this moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may... Number 1 is mostly instrumental style, the second features vocal versus instrument style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/2vAy-1JxLCQ\" data-code=\"2vAy-1JxLCQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/2vAy-1JxLCQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/AfRgD0aTG_Y\" data-code=\"AfRgD0aTG_Y\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/AfRgD0aTG_Y/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T09:35:13-08:00","id":775518,"title":"","content":"Waait, those social-fu charms in Black Claw uses Manipulation.............How OP is the hearthstone that allow you to use Charisma in place of Manipulation ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/772361-how-to-be-a-buff-dispenser-sidereal-machine-in-combat?p=775129#post775129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A poisonous <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iFiiXkonsXY\" target=\"_blank\">kendama </a><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kendama\" target=\"_blank\">hammer-and-ball</a> that is mechanically identical to a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/763801-chain-and-rope-weaponry-peach\">yo-yo</a>? Or just a yo-yo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those type of weapon seem like they will have smashy and flaying Evocation rather than poisonous though. Ooh ooh, but what if the kendama ball is this thing instead <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/c9/76/27/c9762712ffbbaccb6e71a31996329b3b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanandithras</strong> <a href